{"name":"Lunar Federation","hex":"#868381","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lunar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, or resembling the Moon (that is, Luna, the Earth's moon).","Shaped like a crescent moon; lunate."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The middle bone of the proximal series of the carpus in the wrist, which is shaped like a half-moon.","An observation of a lunar distance (“the angle between the Moon and another celestial body”), especially for establishing the longitude of a ship at sea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lunar"},{"term":"federation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of joining together into a single political entity.","An array of nations or states that are unified under one central authority."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an architectural style popular around the time of federation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/federation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Federation","blocks":[{"text":"A federation is a union of partially self-governing provinces, states, or other regions under a federal government (federalism). In a federation, the self-governing status of the component units and the division of power between them and the central government are constitutionally entrenched and may not be altered unilaterally by either the central or constituent-unit authorities without following the constitutional amendment process."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Map_of_unitary_and_federal_states.svg/330px-Map_of_unitary_and_federal_states.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federation","wikidata":"Q43702"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Nigeria_states.png/500px-Nigeria_states.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.